- **Breaking change:** Removed 2017 packs. Hosts no longer receive 2017 packs in their osquery config; only reports are sent. Host details, My device, and report API responses no longer include the `packs` field, and performance stats for 2017 packs are no longer stored. `fleetctl get packs` and `fleetctl upgrade-packs` are no longer available, and `fleetctl apply` and `fleetctl delete` now reject files that contain a `kind: pack` spec. The `/packs`, `/spec/packs`, and pack scheduled query API endpoints were removed and now return 404, including the v1-only `POST /schedule`, `PATCH /schedule/:id`, and `DELETE /schedule/:id` endpoints. `GET /schedule/:id` was removed at every API version and now returns 405 on `2022-04` and later, where the report-backed `PATCH` and `DELETE /schedule/:id` endpoints still exist. The `/schedule` and `/fleets/:fleet_id/schedule` endpoints for reports are unchanged. The hidden packs pages in the UI were removed, so `/packs` URLs now show the 404 page. Upgrading drops the `packs`, `pack_targets`, and `scheduled_queries` tables, logging the names of any 2017 packs it deletes. Before upgrading to Fleet 5, run `fleetctl upgrade-packs` with fleetctl 4 against your Fleet 4 server and apply the output to convert any 2017 packs to reports.
